eval("__webpack_require__.r(__webpack_exports__);\n/* harmony export */ __webpack_require__.d(__webpack_exports__, {\n/* harmony export */   faqs: () => (/* binding */ faqs)\n/* harmony export */ });\nconst faqs = [\n    {\n        q: \"How do I start investing with Zenvest Wealth?\",\n        a: \"It starts with a conversation. We understand your goals, income, existing investments, and risk profile before recommending anything. Once your plan is ready, we help you complete KYC digitally and start SIPs or lump-sum investments within a few days.\"\n    },\n    {\n        q: \"What is the difference between SIP and lump-sum investing?\",\n        a: \"A SIP invests a fixed amount at regular intervals, which averages your purchase cost and enforces discipline. Lump-sum investing deploys a larger amount at once and works best when you have a long horizon and a clear view on valuations. Most portfolios use a combination of both.\"\n    },\n    {\n        q: \"Are mutual funds safe? What are the risks?\",\n        a: \"Mutual funds are regulated by SEBI and offer high transparency, but they are market-linked and can fluctuate in the short term. Risks depend on the category — equity funds are more volatile, debt funds are steadier. We match the risk profile of every fund to your goal horizon.\"\n    },\n    {\n        q: \"How much do I need to start investing?\",\n        a: \"You can start a mutual fund SIP with as little as ₹500 per month. For fixed deposits and bonds, minimums vary by issuer. For PMS, the SEBI-mandated minimum is ₹50 lakh, and AIFs typically require ₹1 crore.\"\n    },\n    {\n        q: \"How are Zenvest's fees structured?\",\n        a: \"As AMFI-registered mutual fund distributors, we earn trail commissions built into the scheme expense ratio — there is no separate fee charged to you for regular plans. For advisory and PMS/AIF onboarding, fees are transparently agreed in writing before you invest.\"\n    },\n    {\n        q: \"Can I withdraw my investments anytime?\",\n        a: \"Most open-ended mutual funds and bank FDs are liquid within a few days, sometimes with a small exit load or penalty. ELSS has a 3-year lock-in, PPF is 15 years, and PMS/AIFs have their own defined lock-ins. We ensure your liquidity ladder is planned in advance.\"\n    },\n    {\n        q: \"How will you review my portfolio?\",\n        a: \"Every Zenvest client gets a scheduled review — typically quarterly for active portfolios and half-yearly for goal-based plans. Reviews cover performance vs. benchmark, allocation drift, tax positioning, and progress toward your goals.\"\n    },\n    {\n        q: \"Do you help with tax planning too?\",\n        a: \"Yes. Tax planning is integrated with your investment plan — not a March-end afterthought. We help optimise Section 80C, 80D, 80CCD, LTCG harvesting, and choice of tax regime, in coordination with your CA where required.\"\n    }\n];\n//# sourceURL=[module]\n//# sourceMappingURL=data:application/json;charset=utf-8;base64,\n//# sourceURL=webpack-internal:///(ssr)/./lib/faq.ts\n");

